WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.240
This is me.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.920
And these are some of my co-workers.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.200
Tonight, we're on an epic adventure,

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.600
defending a village from an army of dog monsters

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.140
and trying not to get ourselves killed.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.550
Welcome to the magical world

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.480
of Dungeons &amp; Dragons,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.520
the best game I've ever played.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.520
Chapter 1: What the f*ck is D&amp;D?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.059
D&amp;D is a tabletop role-playing fantasy game.

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:48.829
You and your friends sit around a table

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:52.839
and pretend to be heroes going on an epic
adventure together.

00:00:52.839 --> 00:00:53.920
This is a role-playing game.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.420
It takes place entirely in our collective
imagination.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.109
Every D&amp;D game is run by a DM -- Dungeon Master.

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:03.569
You arrive at a small village on the outskirts
of the forest.

00:01:03.569 --> 00:01:05.900
The villagers watch you nervously as you enter.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.100
They seem tired, worried.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.280
The DM is the main storyteller in D&amp;D.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:15.780
They create and describe the adventure the
heroes go on,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.409
giving them goals to accomplish

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:19.219
and rewards to motivate them.

00:01:19.219 --> 00:01:20.740
The mayor of this town wants someone

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:25.280
to investigate strange sounds coming from
a nearby abandoned mine.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.460
He's offering a thousand gold pieces to anyone

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.010
brave enough to take the job.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.080
And while it might look like the heroes and
DM

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.460
are playing against each other,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.420
they're actually playing with each other.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.240
The goal of D&amp;D isn't to kill the other players.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.400
There's actually no winning in D&amp;D.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.590
The goal is to hang out with your friends
and

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.240
act like weirdos together.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.810
So the DM's job is to create an adventure
that's

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.500
exciting, fun, and challenging,

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.950
and the heroes' job is to work together to
survive

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.719
those challenges and explore the world the
DM has created.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.420
Which brings me to my favorite part of D&amp;D.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.200
Chapter 2: Creating A Hero.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:02.859
Before you can start adventuring in D&amp;D,

00:02:02.859 --> 00:02:05.399
you need to create your very own hero.

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:07.909
Using the D&amp;D handbook, you pick a race:

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:10.150
human, elf, dwarf, etc.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.380
And you pick a class, basically your job:

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.030
fighter, wizard, rogue.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.390
I play Amelia human warlock.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:18.000
Oneshoe, rock gnome sorcerer.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.520
I play Isla, druid elf.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.440
Harriet, tiefling rogue.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.240
Blaze, dragonborn paladin.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.980
Once you've decided what you want to be,

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.000
you fill out one of these bad boys, a character
sheet,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.000
which is just a piece of paper that keeps
track of

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.560
your strengths and weaknesses.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.560
Stuff like that.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.040
That character sheet is important,

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.640
but way more important is what makes your
hero unique.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.340
Deciding what your hero looks like:

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.820
she has a septum piercing, violet eyes.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.160
She looks like a devil,

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.230
like a fun devil.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.230
Think about Predator.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:46.700
Think Predator in your mind.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.670
How they dress: big sorcerer floppy hat on.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.190
A rotting werewolf pelt.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.060
She doesn't wear a lot of clothing.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.460
And whatever little quirks make them stand
out:

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.590
I hand out pamphlets like a Jehovah's Witness.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.700
I carry a warhammer that's as big as my body.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.180
I have a demonic imp who follows me around.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.140
And what's her name?

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.300
Mother Teresa.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.560
You also create a motivation for your hero,

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.500
something that calls them to adventure.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.730
It can be as lofty as rooting out evil doers

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:13.890
or as simple as

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.980
getting treasure.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.440
Once you've decided who you'll be,

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.600
the DM weaves your stories together and you
start playing.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.450
You pass through the dark entryway of the
abandoned mine.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.370
The passageway is narrow.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:30.290
Suddenly you see a dark figure in the corner.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.340
And you keep playing for a long, long time.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.340
Playing D&amp;D.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.420
I know it seems really complicated,

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.630
and this thickass rulebook doesn't help.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:44.440
But, at its core, all of D&amp;D is just three
steps:

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.549
describe, decide, roll.

00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:49.530
The DM describes what's happening:

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.660
in the corner of the mineshaft you find a
sleeping goblin.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.560
He's lying down on a pile of coins.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.320
He doesn't seem to have noticed you.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.480
What do you do?

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.580
The heroes decide what they want to do:

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.830
I want to steal the coins.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.070
Excellent.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.290
And then the player rolls one of these:

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.520
a 20-sided dice.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.760
Is it dice or die?

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.390
I don't know.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:11.390
Singular of dice.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.050
Historically, dice is the plural of die.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.870
Die is singular, you're right.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.220
I'm going to try it again from earlier on.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.540
And then, the player rolls one of these,

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:20.690
a 20-sided die,

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.900
to find out if they succeeded or failed.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.520
The higher you roll, the better.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.160
I rolled a 2.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.160
Not good.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.250
While sneaking, you knock over a pile of rocks

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.840
and the goblin shoots up wide awake.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.840
Then, the cycle starts over.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.810
The goblin grabs his club, looks at you

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.880
and yells "INTRUDER!"

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.800
What do you do?

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.130
That's D&amp;D in a nutshell.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.810
And it's that second step, "decide,"

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.490
that makes the game so special.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.780
In most games, how you play is limited

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.260
by the options the game designers give you.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:52.440
Run this direction.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.620
Fight this thing.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:54.710
Save this princess.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.150
Essentially being railroaded down a story

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.570
that someone else wrote for you.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:03.400
In D&amp;D, what you do is totally up to you.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.840
Maybe you panic and try to run away.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.060
Maybe you draw your weapon and prepare to
fight.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:09.850
Or maybe you try to trick the goblin.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:18.410
Okay, I look at the goblin and I say "we come
in peace, as friends!"

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:19.540
17?

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.600
The goblin lowers his club, raises his eyebrow,

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.520
and says "friends?"

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.900
The DM sets the stage,

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.389
but once the game starts,

00:05:28.389 --> 00:05:31.090
no one person controls where the story goes.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:32.280
Session after session,

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.931
the DM builds an adventure that

00:05:33.931 --> 00:05:35.770
reflects the heroes choices.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.890
That goblin you tricked last week might tell
you

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.330
about a dragon's lair nearby.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.710
That dragon's lair may contain a valuable
treasure

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:43.840
you can steal.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.020
And stealing that treasure might attract the
attention

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.360
of an evil wizard who wants to use it for
his own schemes.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.760
As the game goes on,

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.620
the decisions you make will shape the world
you play in.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:54.730
We won a karaoke competition.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.600
Closed a rift to the Nine Hells.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.020
We were slaughtering this band of peasants.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.200
It was a total, like, misunderstanding.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.310
D&amp;D doesn't just give you the freedom to choose,

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.740
it asks you to own those choices.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.370
Before long you might find yourself thinking
less like you

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:16.190
and more like the hero you're trying to be.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:19.110
Roleplaying.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.450
All of us are roleplayers.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.830
We go through our lives playing different
parts

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.990
for the people around us.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.730
Some we get to choose.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:28.860
Video producer.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:29.860
Podcaster.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:30.860
Co-worker.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:33.620
Some, we have no control over.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:34.620
Black.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:35.620
Female.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.620
Queer.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.980
Even with our friends, we can fall into patterns
of behavior

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:42.040
that eventually become expectations.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.090
The wisecracker.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.090
The cool girl.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.110
The shy one.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.240
Roles we're so used to playing

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.480
we don't even think of them as roles anymore.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.850
They're just us.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:54.260
D&amp;D gives you permission to be something different.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.889
To surprise yourself.

00:06:55.889 --> 00:06:57.570
And that can be really scary.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.660
When you do something in D&amp;D,

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.620
We come in peace!

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.490
you're trusting everyone at the table to take
you seriously.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.970
And you're trusting the other players to have
your back.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:09.280
I pull a flower out of my hair,

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.889
hand it to him and give him a wink.

00:07:10.889 --> 00:07:13.770
I produce tiny rainbow over Harriet's head?

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:16.480
Mother Teresa does her best goblin impression
and says

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:18.440
"it's cool, they're with me."

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.440
16.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.440
18.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.190
Natural 20.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.810
The goblin looks at you more relaxed and says

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:27.570
"FRIENDS!"

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:31.010
That shared vulnerability is what makes D&amp;D
different

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.860
from any other game you play with your friends.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:36.740
We can spend our whole lives wandering alone

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:39.020
through the corridors of our minds.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.360
D&amp;D asks you to wander together.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.600
To believe, for just a few hours,

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.229
that there is more to us than what meets the
eye.

00:07:47.229 --> 00:07:48.229
More silliness.

00:07:48.229 --> 00:07:49.229
More warmth.

00:07:49.229 --> 00:07:50.960
More bravery.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:55.480
And yeah, just a little more magic.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:58.880
Should you play D&amp;D?

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.500
D&amp;D is ridiculous.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.480
But when I ask my friends why they play D&amp;D,

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.750
they don't talk about the monsters or the
dungeons.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.729
They talk about how the game makes them feel.

00:08:12.729 --> 00:08:14.600
It just feels so freeing.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.540
I'm not thinking about, you know,

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.120
I have to do this tomorrow or I need to take
care of this at home.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.290
It just kind of, like, brings your inner child
back out.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.820
Nobody makes fun of anybody.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.260
Nobody feels self-conscious about it.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:26.520
The older that you get,

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.970
the more expectations people have of you.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.639
D&amp;D, there aren't any expectations.

00:08:30.639 --> 00:08:32.459
I can just be free.

00:08:32.459 --> 00:08:34.659
I feel like the rest of the world doesn't
matter,

00:08:34.659 --> 00:08:36.409
like, I'm always super stoked to play.

00:08:36.409 --> 00:08:39.729
It's like a fun, really creative way to connect
with each other.

00:08:39.729 --> 00:08:41.219
It's made us really grow closer.

00:08:41.219 --> 00:08:42.409
The way that you look at the people you were

00:08:42.409 --> 00:08:44.920
just playing with is really different than
other people

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.360
in the real world because you've engaged in
something

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.199
so collaborative and imagined together.

00:08:50.199 --> 00:08:53.319
The point of D&amp;D is obviously, like, adventures
and

00:08:53.319 --> 00:08:55.529
"oh we're world-building together!"

00:08:55.529 --> 00:08:57.720
But the real point of D&amp;D is, like,

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:58.889
you're in this bubble with these people

00:08:58.889 --> 00:09:00.790
and you're entirely focused on each other

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:03.279
and remembering all the reasons that you like

00:09:03.279 --> 00:09:05.339
spending time with their characters but also

00:09:05.339 --> 00:09:07.439
spending time with them as human beings.

00:09:07.439 --> 00:09:09.350
If you look past the wizards,

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:11.410
past the dungeons and magical creatures,

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:15.389
D&amp;D is a game about the people you play with.

00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:18.600
A game where everyone agrees to bring their
weirdness

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.649
and creativity to the table.

00:09:20.649 --> 00:09:22.529
Byrd, not now.

00:09:22.529 --> 00:09:25.380
To help build a world that belongs to all
of you.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.930
A world shaped by your triumphs, your defeats,

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:33.649
your personality quirks, and your stupid inside
jokes.

00:09:33.649 --> 00:09:36.240
A world that could not have existed

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.980
if you and your friends hadn't sat down

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.720
at a table one day and said

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:46.079
"let's play."

00:09:46.079 --> 00:09:48.939
Believe it or not, this video is not sponsored
by D&amp;D.

00:09:48.939 --> 00:09:50.439
We're just huge nerds.

00:09:50.439 --> 00:09:51.490
But if you're interested in playing,

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.649
you should check out the D&amp;D starter set.

00:09:53.649 --> 00:09:56.139
It comes with a premade campaign, character
sheets,

00:09:56.139 --> 00:09:57.680
a mini rulebook, and dice.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.519
And if you're interested in seeing more videos
about games,

00:10:00.519 --> 00:10:01.820
check out our sister site Polygon.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:04.559
They have this cool new series called Fiend
Zone

00:10:04.559 --> 00:10:08.709
which talks about how games shape and reflect
our culture.

00:10:08.709 --> 00:10:10.550
Killed it that time.

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:11.680
That's a wrap baby.

